{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JYbJfrx3QxRsMSmgHWzYjz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-552\"\n3\ttitle = \"The adjudicator's two exits: adjudication-row close, successor mint, OI mint with refusal invariant (OI-70)\"\n4\tspecref = \"docs/requirements/open-items.toml#OI-70\"\n5\tworkstream = \"process\"\n6\tsr_refs = [\"SR-144\"]\n7\tneeds = []\n8\tbuildtier = \"strong\"\n9\tsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n10\tpriority = 3\n11\t+++\n12\t\n13\t## Context\n14\t\n15\t`OI-70` RULED 2026-08-31 (record `docs/log.d/2026-08-31-owner-rulings-oi70-71-72.md`,\n16\tcompiled into `docs/log.md`): partial is the only stop, every closure produces\n17\ta handback, and the adjudicator judging that handback has exactly two exits —\n18\ta QUEUED successor WI where the work continues by another route, and/or a\n19\tminted OPEN ITEM where the answer is human-owed. Mixed outcomes are permitted;\n20\t`deferred/` is never an adjudicator destination unless what it places there is\n21\ta replacement.\n22\t\n23\tWhat exists: `handback.close_partial` writes the immutable report (`LLR-144`),\n24\t`intake._close_drafts` mints exactly one disposition row per report\n25\t(`LLR-161`), and ADJUDICATE sessions draft successors (`WI-550` drafted\n26\t`WI-551`). What is missing (decision 21 of\n27\t`docs/decisions-for-review-2026-08-31.md` carries the live evidence): the\n28\tADJUDICATE brief promises \"the machinery mints your draft at this row's own\n29\tclose\" and NOTHING performs that close — the dispatcher resumes a finished\n30\tadjudication row in a cycle until a supervisor closes it by hand.\n31\t\n32\tRE-SCOPED by `OI-73`, RULED 2026-08-31 (record\n33\t`docs/log.d/2026-08-31-owner-ruling-oi73.md`), same-day refinement of OI-70's\n34\texits: a successor is MANDATORY at every partial/cancelled close (the\n35\tOI-alone exit is retired); a minted OI becomes a typed hard dependency of the\n36\tsuccessor rather than a standalone exit; the mint REPLACES the superseded\n37\trow's inbound hard `needs` edges; and `OI-###` ids become valid hard tokens\n38\tin `needs`, satisfied when the row leaves `pending`. Done-when 2–4 below are\n39\tamended and 5–6 added accordingly.\n40\t\n41\t## Done-when\n42\t\n43\t1. An adjudication row whose session recorded a verdict CLOSES mechanically:\n44\t   its `## Dispositions` successor drafts are minted into `queued/` (ids from\n45\t   the watermark, `spec_move.py` for every move), the row archives terminal,\n46\t   and the dispatcher no longer resumes it.\n47\t2. The human-owed arm exists: the close can mint an OPEN ITEM row into\n48\t   `docs/requirements/open-items.toml` — id from the watermark's OI space,\n49\t   `status = \"pending\"`, `gen_open_items.py` regenerated in the same commit —\n50\t   and the minted id lands in the queued successor's `needs`, so the ruling\n51\t   gates the successor's readiness instead of relying on adjudicator\n52\t   restraint (OI-73).\n53\t3. The refusal invariant (as tightened by OI-73): a PARTIAL or CANCELLED\n54\t   disposition that queues NO successor is REFUSED at the close — an OI alone\n55\t   no longer discharges it; no third exit, nothing silent.\n56\t4. The mint REPLACES the inbound hard `needs` edges of the row the successor\n57\t   supersedes (`supersedes` is the carrier) — the `WI-541` strand class (its\n58\t   `needs` waited on a terminal row) becomes unrepresentable, not merely\n59\t   visible (OI-73's replacement-not-report arm).\n60\t5. Typed OI edges: an `OI-###` id is a valid HARD token in `needs` —\n61\t   existence validated through the spine carrier and the id-watermark's OI\n62\t   space, readiness satisfied when the row leaves `pending` (a new waiting\n63\t   reason in the scheduler), the template grammar and PROCESS_OPTIONS\n64\t   dependency prose widened TOLERANTLY so bare WI ids keep meaning what they\n65\t   mean and no downstream registry migrates.\n66\t6. The validator net: `dead_dependency_findings` extends to `partial`\n67\t   predecessors, so a strand minted outside this path is reported rather than\n68\t   silent.\n69\t7. Tests drive all six on a scaffold, and the ADJUDICATE brief's contract\n70\t   text matches what the machinery now actually does.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452717b7-58f1-46bc-b7da-1c8e304ffaa5","uuid":"c794dcff-590f-485f-a2bd-44eae94b1269","timestamp":"2026-09-01T06:26:33.610Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/wi-552-adjudicator-two-exit-close/docs/work/active/wi-552-adjudicator-two-exit-close/WI-552-adjudicator-two-exit-close.md","content":"+++\nid = \"WI-552\"\ntitle = \"The adjudicator's two exits: adjudication-row close, successor mint, OI mint with refusal invariant (OI-70)\"\nspecref = \"docs/requirements/open-items.toml#OI-70\"\nworkstream = \"process\"\nsr_refs = [\"SR-144\"]\nneeds = []\nbuildtier = \"strong\"\nsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\npriority = 3\n+++\n\n## Context\n\n`OI-70` RULED 2026-08-31 (record `docs/log.d/2026-08-31-owner-rulings-oi70-71-72.md`,\ncompiled into `docs/log.md`): partial is the only stop, every closure produces\na handback, and the adjudicator judging that handback has exactly two exits —\na QUEUED successor WI where the work continues by another route, and/or a\nminted OPEN ITEM where the answer is human-owed. Mixed outcomes are permitted;\n`deferred/` is never an adjudicator destination unless what it places there is\na replacement.\n\nWhat exists: `handback.close_partial` writes the immutable report (`LLR-144`),\n`intake._close_drafts` mints exactly one disposition row per report\n(`LLR-161`), and ADJUDICATE sessions draft successors (`WI-550` drafted\n`WI-551`). What is missing (decision 21 of\n`docs/decisions-for-review-2026-08-31.md` carries the live evidence): the\nADJUDICATE brief promises \"the machinery mints your draft at this row's own\nclose\" and NOTHING performs that close — the dispatcher resumes a finished\nadjudication row in a cycle until a supervisor closes it by hand.\n\nRE-SCOPED by `OI-73`, RULED 2026-08-31 (record\n`docs/log.d/2026-08-31-owner-ruling-oi73.md`), same-day refinement of OI-70's\nexits: a successor is MANDATORY at every partial/cancelled close (the\nOI-alone exit is retired); a minted OI becomes a typed hard dependency of the\nsuccessor rather than a standalone exit; the mint REPLACES the superseded\nrow's inbound hard `needs` edges; and `OI-###` ids become valid hard tokens\nin `needs`, satisfied when the row leaves `pending`. Done-when 2–4 below are\namended and 5–6 added accordingly.\n\n## Done-when\n\n1. An adjudication row whose session recorded a verdict CLOSES mechanically:\n   its `## Dispositions` successor drafts are minted into `queued/` (ids from\n   the watermark, `spec_move.py` for every move), the row archives terminal,\n   and the dispatcher no longer resumes it.\n2. The human-owed arm exists: the close can mint an OPEN ITEM row into\n   `docs/requirements/open-items.toml` — id from the watermark's OI space,\n   `status = \"pending\"`, `gen_open_items.py` regenerated in the same commit —\n   and the minted id lands in the queued successor's `needs`, so the ruling\n   gates the successor's readiness instead of relying on adjudicator\n   restraint (OI-73).\n3. The refusal invariant (as tightened by OI-73): a PARTIAL or CANCELLED\n   disposition that queues NO successor is REFUSED at the close — an OI alone\n   no longer discharges it; no third exit, nothing silent.\n4. The mint REPLACES the inbound hard `needs` edges of the row the successor\n   supersedes (`supersedes` is the carrier) — the `WI-541` strand class (its\n   `needs` waited on a terminal row) becomes unrepresentable, not merely\n   visible (OI-73's replacement-not-report arm).\n5. Typed OI edges: an `OI-###` id is a valid HARD token in `needs` —\n   existence validated through the spine carrier and the id-watermark's OI\n   space, readiness satisfied when the row leaves `pending` (a new waiting\n   reason in the scheduler), the template grammar and PROCESS_OPTIONS\n   dependency prose widened TOLERANTLY so bare WI ids keep meaning what they\n   mean and no downstream registry migrates.\n6. The validator net: `dead_dependency_findings` extends to `partial`\n   predecessors, so a strand minted outside this path is reported rather than\n   silent.\n7. Tests drive all six on a scaffold, and the ADJUDICATE brief's contract\n   text matches what the machinery now actually does.\n","numLines":71,"startLine":1,"totalLines":71}}}
